WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.769
At the AlegrIA hackathon, organized by Cashea and

2
00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:06.769
Yummy, we had a talk — online, at least

3
00:00:06.769 --> 00:00:10.615
— with Pedro Vallenilla, the co-founder of Cashea,

4
00:00:10.615 --> 00:00:14.769
and months later he came to give that same talk, well,

5
00:00:14.769 --> 00:00:17.000
an improved, much fuller one,

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
in Barquisimeto in person, with Father Elías Sayegh.

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.931
And we were literally in the theater's second row,

8
00:00:27.931 --> 00:00:30.010
right in front.

9
00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:34.580
He told how several of his startups failed before

10
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:39.150
Cashea's huge success, with a family and in debt,

11
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:44.000
and he still kept going, and going, and made Cashea.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.910
What stayed with me most is how he talks about

13
00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:51.820
Venezuela: after everything it's been through,

14
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.880
it's a greenfield to build anything,

15
00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.555
because the tech solutions other countries already have

16
00:00:59.555 --> 00:01:01.000
just aren't here.

17
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.507
That's why Venezuela, in theory,

18
00:01:04.507 --> 00:01:09.000
is at the best moment to build a company.

19
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.038
Well, not in theory: in practice.
